   "fix": "Add `@[simp]` to `one_sub_blackDisc`. The in-file use at :153 is `rw [one_sub_blackDisc]` and is unaffected; the LHS pattern is closed (no higher-order metavariables) and the RHS contains no `blackDisc`, so it cannot loop.",
   "issue": "`one_sub_blackDisc` \u2014 the characteristic S-matrix identity of the black disc, `Matrix.of (fun x y => 1 - blackDisc x y) = 1` \u2014 carries no `@[simp]`, while the parallel lemma for the other witness, `one_sub_golecBiernatWusthoff` (:171), is `@[simp]`. The RHS `1` is strictly simpler and eliminates both `Matrix.of` and `blackDisc`, so this is a normal-form rewrite; consumers must `rw` it by hand in exactly the position (`(Matrix.of fun x y => 1 - N x y).PosSemidef`, the shape of `IsAdmissible.posSemidef_one_sub` at :90) where it arises.",
